1. Document Structure
Tag	Description
<html>	The root element that encapsulates the entire HTML document.
<head>	Contains meta-information, title, and links to stylesheets (invisible to users).
<title>	Defines the title of the document shown in the browser tab.
<body>	Contains all the visible content displayed on the webpage.
2. Text & Headings
Tag	Description
<h1> to <h6>	Define headings. <h1> is the most important main title, down to <h6>.
<p>	Defines a paragraph or block of regular text.
<span>	A generic inline container used to style a specific part of text.
3. Containers & Layout
Tag	Description
<div>	A generic block-level container used to group elements together for styling or layout.
    4. Links & Media
Tag	Description
<a>	Defines a hyperlink. Use the href="..." attribute to specify the URL destination.
<img>	Embeds an image. Requires src="..." for the image path and alt="..." for text description.

5. Lists
Tag	Description
<ul>	Defines an unordered (bulleted) list.
<ol>	Defines an ordered (numbered) list.
<li>	Defines a specific list item inside a <ul> or <ol>.
6. Forms & Interaction
Tag	Description
<form>	A container for user input fields, used to collect and submit data.
<input>	An input field where users can enter data. Controlled by the type="..." attribute (e.g., text, email).
<label>	Defines a text label for an <input> element, improving accessibility.

    Tag	Description
<button>	Defines a clickable button that can submit a form or trigger JavaScript.
    1. Typography & Text
color	Controls the color of text.
font-size	Defines the size of the text.
font-family	Sets the typeface (font) used for text.
font-weight	Controls how bold text appears.
text-align	Aligns text horizontally (left, center, right).
line-height	Controls vertical spacing between lines of text.
text-decoration	Adds underline, overline, or line-through.
2. Box Model & Sizing
width	Sets the horizontal width of an element.
height	Sets the vertical height of an element.
margin	Creates transparent space outside an element.
padding	Creates space inside an element (around content).
border	Adds a border around an element (e.g., 1px solid black).
border-radius	Rounds the outer corners of an element.

4. Positioning
position	Defines positioning method (relative, absolute, fixed).
top / left / ...	Moves positioned elements away from their edges.

5. Backgrounds & Visuals
background-color	Sets the solid background color of an element.
background-image	Applies an image as the background.
background-size	Controls how background images scale (cover, contain).
box-shadow	Adds a drop-shadow around an element.
opacity	Controls transparency (0.0 is hidden, 1.0 is solid).
6. Interactivity & Motion
cursor	Changes the mouse cursor appearance (e.g., pointer).